## Learnings from 2026-04-04 Session (Website visual regression)

1. **`website-qa` gate order** — **Gate 0:** **`bun run design:audit`** (principles in `.cursor/rules/design-principles.mdc`, skill `.cursor/skills/design-audit.md`) → **Gate 1:** **`bun run test:website`** (`agent-browser` pixel diff vs `test-engine/website-baselines/`) → **Gate 2:** **`bun run website:lighthouse`**. Refresh goldens after intentional layout/CSS changes with **`bun run test:website:update`**.
2. **One-time browser** — After `bun install`, run `./node_modules/.bin/agent-browser install` once per machine so Chrome for Testing is available.
3. **Pretext + demo section** — Sections containing `.rift-demo-window` must **skip** `layoutPage()` padding overrides; otherwise Pretext padding plus `min-height` on the demo reads as a large empty white box.
4. **Tech quartet grid** — Use explicit **4 / 2 / 1** column breakpoints (e.g. 900px / 500px), not `auto-fit` + `minmax`, to avoid a **3+1** orphan row around ~960px.
5. **`agent-browser eval --json`** wraps results as `{ success, data: { result } }` — extract `data.result` (see `scripts/design-audit-extract-json.js`). Do not use `node <<HEREDOC "$file"` with extra args — **node treats the first arg as the script file**; use a `.js` file or env vars instead.
6. **Story section (`#story`)** — Prefer scannable **`.story-block`** blocks (`.story-condition` label + `.story-desc` with `data-pretext`) plus a **`.story-kicker`** line instead of long `.story-line` essay paragraphs. Gate 0 programmatic checks in `scripts/design-audit-eval.js` target **`p.story-desc` / `p.story-kicker`** inside `.story-body`.